                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Before expensive skins, fancy matchmaking, and esports celebrities, there was Counter-Strike 1.6.\n\nNo distractions. Just you, your AK-47, de_dust2, and a suspiciously talented 12-year-old destroying your entire team.\n\nThe gameplay is beautifully simple. Easy to understand, brutally difficult to master. The gunplay, movement, legendary maps, and community servers made this game unforgettable.\n\nSure, the graphics look ancient, the learning curve is ruthless, and public servers could be a fascinating experiment in human behavior. But none of that stopped millions of people from playing for ridiculous amounts of time.\n\nThe Good:\n\nTimeless, skill-based gunplay.\n\nLegendary maps that never get old.\n\nCommunity servers and hilarious multiplayer memories.\n\nRuns on practically anything with electricity.\n\nThe Bad:\n\nGraphics belong in a museum.\n\nUnforgiving for beginners.\n\nCheaters and questionable server experiences.\n\nLacks modern matchmaking conveniences.\n\nMy Ratings:\n\nGameplay: 9.5/10\n\nGraphics: 5/10\n\nReplayability: 10/10\n\nEnjoyment: 9.5/10\n\nOverall: 9/10\n\nFinal Verdict:\n\nCounter-Strike 1.6 didn't need fancy graphics or a battle pass to keep people hooked.\n\nJust two teams, one bomb, and someone screaming “RUSH B” like their family's future depended on it.\n\nAn absolute multiplayer legend.",
